        "title": "Apple strikes deal with AI startup that lets musicians rework recorded music",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/19/apple-strikes-deal-with-ai-startup-that-lets-musicians-rework-recorded-music/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/10/samplab.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The EU’s List of Acquisitions website was updated today with details of a deal struck in June between Apple and Samplab, a Swiss startup that described itself as offering “music production for the age of AI.” Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1074861\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/19/apple-strikes-deal-with-ai-startup-that-lets-musicians-rework-recorded-music/#more-1074861\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
